# Requests for every endpoint of Loki.Samples.WebApi (Visual Studio, Rider, or VS Code with the REST Client extension).
# Start the databases and the API first (see samples/README.md). {{engine}} is sqlserver or oracle.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@engine = sqlserver

### Registered Loki providers, and which engines have a connection string
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/engines

### Row counts of the sample tables
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{engine}}/counts

### Models: IEnumerable<CustomerImportRow> with a ModelMapping (FullName -> Name, ...)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{engine}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "name": "Ada Lovelace", "email": "ada@example.com" },
  { "name": "Alan Turing", "email": null }
]

### DataTable: TableName "ProductImport" selects the ProductImportMapping DataMapping
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{engine}}/products/datatable?count=5000

### IDataReader: SaveAsync(reader, "Products", sourceName: "ProductImport")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{engine}}/products/reader?count=5000

### JSON upload: SaveAsync(stream, "Products"). The payload's tableName is ignored; RequireDataMappingForJson limits the columns.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{engine}}/json/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableName": "Orders",
  "columns": [
    { "name": "Sku", "type": "string" },
    { "name": "Name", "type": "string" },
    { "name": "Price", "type": "decimal" },
    { "name": "NotMapped", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "data": [
    { "Sku": "JSON-1", "Name": "Desk lamp", "Price": 24.99, "NotMapped": "never copied" },
    { "Sku": "JSON-2", "Name": "Notebook", "Price": 3.5, "NotMapped": null }
  ]
}

### JSON upload into Customers
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{engine}}/json/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableName": "Customers",
  "columns": [
    { "name": "Name", "type": "string" },
    { "name": "Email", "type": "string" },
    { "name": "CreatedOn", "type": "datetime" }
  ],
  "data": [
    { "Name": "Grace Hopper", "Email": "grace@example.com", "CreatedOn": "2026-11-22T10:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### JSON upload into a table that is not on the allow-list: 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{engine}}/json/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tableName": "Orders", "columns": [], "data": [] }

### Send the JSON upload again: the SKUs already exist, 409 and nothing saved
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{engine}}/json/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableName": "Products",
  "columns": [ { "name": "Sku", "type": "string" }, { "name": "Name", "type": "string" }, { "name": "Price", "type": "decimal" } ],
  "data": [ { "Sku": "JSON-1", "Name": "Desk lamp", "Price": 24.99 } ]
}

### SQL Server: EF Core and Loki in one caller-owned transaction, committed by the caller
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sqlserver/customers-with-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Margaret Hamilton", "email": "margaret@example.com", "orderCount": 2500, "simulateFailure": false }

### SQL Server: the same, failing after Loki's save: the caller rolls back, neither the customer nor the orders are saved (500)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sqlserver/customers-with-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Rolled back", "email": null, "orderCount": 2500, "simulateFailure": true }

### Oracle: direct-path load into the staging table, then INSERT ... SELECT into Products
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/oracle/products/staging-import?count=20000

### Oracle: a duplicate SKU loads into staging, but the move into Products fails (409) and the batch is discarded
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/oracle/products/staging-import?count=100&includeDuplicate=true
